bilbo remember: keep files as entries, and what grew or changed in them since.

[1mUsage:[22m
  [36mbilbo remember [39m[2m<file|folder>[22m[36m [--kind [39m[2m<kind>[22m[36m] [--follow][39m
  [36mbilbo remember[39m
  [36mbilbo remember --hook[39m

[1mOptions:[22m
      [1m--kind [22m[2m<kind>[22m  Run this kind, not the one that claims the files
      [1m--follow[22m       Save the target in the config file, so a bare run keeps it
      [1m--hook[22m         Keep the transcript a harness hook names on stdin

[1mKinds:[22m
  [1mmarkdown[22m  .md files, one record per line
  [1msession[22m   Claude Code and Codex sessions, one record per JSONL line

[1mOutput:[22m
  new [2m<n>[22m, appended [2m<n>[22m, new generation [2m<n>[22m, unchanged [2m<n>[22m, refused [2m<n>[22m
  records [2m<n>[22m, raw bytes [2m<n>[22m, stored bytes [2m<n>[22m

[1mExit:[22m
  [1m0[22m  success, and --hook once it runs
  [1m1[22m  a refused file, nothing to keep, a missing target, a store or index failure
  [1m2[22m  usage or config error, or a config file --follow cannot write

[1mExamples:[22m
  [36mbilbo remember ~/.claude/projects --kind session[39m
  [36mbilbo remember ~/notes --follow[39m

[1mDocs:[22m [2mhttps://github.com/delucca/bilbo/wiki/Commands#remember[22m
